{"sections":[{"type":"Header","label":"Select another area to see whether students stayed or left ","content":"<h2>How many people stayed in Preesall after gaining qualifications?</h2>"},{"type":"ResultsMap","content":"<p>Preesall is a <b>small town</b>  in <b>the North West</b>. Preesall does not have its own university.</p><p>Preesall has higher levels of deprivation.</p>"},{"type":"ResultsOverall","content":"<p></p>"},{"type":"Highlight","content":"<p><b>Note:</b>  all towns and cities in this analysis are defined based on population size only. This means that some cities are classed as towns because of their population.</p>"},{"type":"Results","content":"<h4>Let's explore this further</h4><p>There were 230 state-school pupils from Preesall who sat their GCSEs between the 2007 to 2008 and the 2010 to 2011 school years. </p><p>Of these, 75 (33%) went on to gain degree-level qualifications (<a href=\"https://www.gov.uk/what-different-qualification-levels-mean/list-of-qualification-levels\">level 6+ as defined by The Office of Qualifications and Examinations Regulation, or Ofqual</a> ). We will call these people <a href=\"https://www.ons.gov.uk/peoplepopulationandcommunity/educationandchildcare/articles/geographicalmobilityofyoungpeopleacrossenglishtownsandcities/march2024#glossary\">graduates</a>. </p><p>Another 90 (39%) went on to gain other advanced post-16 qualifications, such as A-Levels, a foundation degree or higher apprenticeship (levels 3-5 as defined by Ofqual). In this tool, we will refer to these non-graduates with advanced qualifications as “qualified non-graduates\", for brevity. </p><p>The charts below compare Preesall to other English towns and cities using three measures: <ul><li>what proportion of Preesall's pupils became graduates or qualified non-graduates by the 2017 to 2018 academic year</li><li>of those graduates and qualified non-graduates, the percentages that lived in Preesall in the 2018 to 2019 academic year</li><li>how many graduates and qualified non-graduates from elsewhere came to live there by 2018 to 2019, relative to the number who sat their GCSEs there  </li></ul></p><p>In some towns, some of this information may not be available because of small sample sizes. </p>"},{"type":"BarcodeSummary"},{"type":"Section","content":"<p>The size and deprivation level of a town, as well as the qualification levels of older residents, were all related to students' educational attainment. <a href=\"https://www.ons.gov.uk/peoplepopulationandcommunity/educationandchildcare/articles/whydochildrenandyoungpeopleinsmallertownsdobetteracademicallythanthoseinlargertowns/2023-07-25\">Read our previous analysis.</a>  </p>"},{"type":"Section","content":"<p> </p>"},{"type":"Section","content":"<p> </p>"},{"type":"Section","content":"<p></p>"},{"type":"Section","content":"<p> </p>"},{"type":"Section","content":"<p></p>"}],"place":{"areacd":"E34004474","areanm":"Preesall","parentcd":"E34004474","size":"small town","region":"the North West","university":"No University","cohort":230,"grads":75,"grads_perc":0.326086957,"skilled":90,"skilled_perc":0.391304348,"grads_net_perc":"*","skilled_net_perc":"*","grads_left":45,"grads_left_perc":0.6,"grads_left_BUA_same_ttwa":"*","grads_left_BUA_same_ttwa_perc":"*","grads_region_move":"*","grads_region_move_perc":"*","grads_moved_popular_region":"*","grads_moved_popular_region_tie":"*","skilled_left":40,"skilled_left_perc":0.444444444,"attraction_grad":"*","retention_grad":0.4,"participation_grad":0.326086957,"attraction_skilled":"*","retention_skilled":0.555555556,"participation_skilled":0.391304348,"TTWA_name":"Blackpool","grad_net_rank":"*","skilled_net_rank":0,"deprivation":"higher","grads_1819_total":"*","grads_1819_homegrown_perc":"*","grads_1819_migrants_perc":"*","skilled_1819_total":"*","skilled_1819_homegrown_perc":"*","skilled_1819_migrants_perc":"*","skilled_Moved_region_1819":"*","skilled_left_BUA_same_ttwa":30,"skilled_left_BUA_same_ttwa_perc":0.75,"grads_stayed_TTWA_for